        {
          "do": "inspect",
          "kicker": "Blogs",
          "title": "Building Weird Little Things",
          "text": "Skye writes about using AI to learn unfamiliar skills and begin building ideas without already knowing every technical detail.\n\n“You can start with an idea instead of a perfect plan. You can say, “I want something inspired by a retro handheld companion, but not a copy. No arms. No legs. Just a face screen, buttons, a speaker, and a printable shell.” Then AI can help translate that vague shape into something more concrete: proportions, display size, vents, button placement, Raspberry Pi clearance, sensor holes, USB-C access, screw posts, and shell seams.”\n\n— AI Makes Building Weird Little Things Possible Again"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "book-library_blog_portland",
      "kind": "inspect",
      "label": "A City Worth Exploring",
      "at": [
