          "id": "library_blog_portland"
        },
        {
          "do": "inspect",
          "kicker": "Blogs",
          "title": "A City Worth Exploring",
          "text": "Skye argues for making Portland’s existing businesses and culture easier to reach.\n\n“The city should stop treating that identity like an accidental side effect and start building an economic strategy around it.\nNot by turning every neighborhood into a tourist trap. Not by replacing what people like with a row of chain stores, branded murals, and $19 cocktails named after the color beige. I mean making it easier for people to find, reach, and spend money at the places that already make Portland worth visiting.”\n\n— How I Would Fix Portland: Stop Treating It Like It Has Nothing to Offer"
        }
      ]
    },
