        },
        {
          "do": "inspect",
          "kicker": "Blogs",
          "title": "Designing a Night Out",
          "text": "Skye examines how venue design shapes the experience of going out.\n\n“Instead, many Portland bars and clubs feel like they were assembled with almost no thought about how people actually experience them.\nNot because the owners don't care, but because design decisions compound into an experience that feels frustrating before the night even begins.”\n\n— Portland’s Nightlife Doesn’t Have a People Problem. It Has a Design Problem."
        }
      ]
